WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:01.630
- Your friend Ashton Kutcher

00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:04.050
became literally my
marker to all my friends.

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:07.647
I was like, "If any of you ever
put me on that show Punk'D,

00:00:07.647 --> 00:00:10.080
"I will never speak to you again."

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:13.510
Because it is, you know
what I hate in life?

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:16.070
As much as I'm like a scrappy cat,

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:18.240
I do not like gotcha moments.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:22.130
Don't let me work my entire
life to be a good person

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:25.221
and then nail me in a corner

00:00:25.221 --> 00:00:28.057
by poking me like an
animal and then going,

00:00:28.057 --> 00:00:30.887
"Oh, that's who she really is.

00:00:30.887 --> 00:00:33.027
"We knew, we knew it, it's fake.

00:00:33.027 --> 00:00:35.160
"She's not a good person, she's a jerk."

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.600
But I do love Ashton
Kutcher, nothing against him.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.981
But boy, that show really scared me.

00:00:39.981 --> 00:00:41.983
- When then your gonna hate
this. Ashton, come on out!

00:00:41.983 --> 00:00:44.950
(Drew laughing)
No, I'm just kidding.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:49.353
- Okay, there is a "That
'90s Show" revival.

00:00:49.353 --> 00:00:50.372
- There is, yeah.

00:00:50.372 --> 00:00:52.870
(audience cheering)

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:56.590
It's starring Deborah Jo
Rupp who played my mom

00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:57.550
and Kurtwood Smith,

00:00:57.550 --> 00:00:59.990
and they're great friends
of mine and amazing people,

00:00:59.990 --> 00:01:03.000
and a whole new group of kids, yeah.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.550
- Okay, tell me about the
show that you are in now.

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:07.390
Second season, big hit,

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:09.857
really respected, great reviews.

00:01:09.857 --> 00:01:11.220
"Home Economics."

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:14.440
- I love it. It's-
(audience clapping)

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:16.000
This cast is,

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.930
yeah, I really feel like I was
part of a dream team before

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:22.220
and I was so nervous because of COVID.

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:23.380
I'd met all of them

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:26.560
but I hadn't been in the same
room with all of us together.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:27.760
It's like dating or something.

00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:28.773
At first you go,

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:31.090
you can't predict it,

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:32.670
you don't know until you show up.

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:35.460
And the first day I went
to work I was so nervous.

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:36.850
And then about two days in,

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:39.899
I was driving home and I
was just straight up cocky.

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:41.670
They're so great.

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:43.080
I was like, "I don't even
have to do anything."

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:44.510
They're just my favorite group of people.

00:01:44.510 --> 00:01:46.910
- Well, there is another television show

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:48.643
that I heard you are a fan of.

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:51.370
- Okay, yeah. I mean, yeah.

00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:54.090
Look, I'm into "The Bachelor," okay.

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:56.270
I wasn't originally.

00:01:56.270 --> 00:01:59.400
I started dating a girl,
she became my wife,

00:01:59.400 --> 00:02:01.890
and she pushed it on me.

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:05.390
And then a couple years
into it I started to realize

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:06.317
when I was out of town I was like

00:02:06.317 --> 00:02:07.897
"Well, you're not gonna
watch it tonight, right?

00:02:07.897 --> 00:02:09.940
"Can you like, wait until,"

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:12.760
which, by the way, I
missed "Women Tell All."

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:15.840
- Okay, what are you
thinking prediction-wise

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:16.998
that's gonna happen,

00:02:16.998 --> 00:02:19.450
'cause we're almost at
the end of the season.

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:21.490
- I know, without
watching "Women Tell All"

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:25.600
I'm hesitant to make any firm predictions.

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:29.530
- Well, there is someone actually here

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:31.370
that we have as a surprise for you

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:33.910
who I think can fill in some blanks.

00:02:33.910 --> 00:02:34.743
- Who?

00:02:34.743 --> 00:02:37.267
- Oh, it's just the host
of the show, Jesse Palmer.

00:02:37.267 --> 00:02:42.267
(upbeat music)
(audience cheering)

00:02:46.827 --> 00:02:50.037
- How are you (indistinct)?

00:02:50.037 --> 00:02:50.870
I know.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:52.560
I'm not Ashton Kutcher.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.763
- [Topher] She just said
she hates gotcha moments.

00:02:55.647 --> 00:02:57.270
- But this is a good one!

00:02:57.270 --> 00:02:59.973
- I'll squeeze on in.
- We're not gonna tease you.

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:02.096
- That's why when Tom Cruise-

00:03:02.096 --> 00:03:03.440
- No, this is an amazing surprise.

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:05.558
It's great to meet you, man.

00:03:05.558 --> 00:03:07.330
- Listen, just like your childhood,

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:09.130
I was drinking in a parking garage

00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:10.370
down the street here in New York,

00:03:10.370 --> 00:03:12.920
and I heard that you were
this big fan of the show.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:14.520
So on behalf of the Bachelor Nation,

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:16.400
I just wanted to to stop by and say

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:17.900
thank you, man, appreciate it.

00:03:18.877 --> 00:03:20.177
- You gotta do me a favor.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:24.870
You gotta look into the camera
and say hello to my wife.

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:26.270
I'll get so many brownie points.

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:27.847
Say "Hello, Ashley Grace."

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:30.370
She's so jealous right, go ahead.

00:03:30.370 --> 00:03:32.150
- Ashley Grace,

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:34.738
will you accept Topher's final rose?

00:03:34.738 --> 00:03:37.821
(audience cheering)

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:41.590
- I also wanna say hi to my friend Wendy

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:43.860
because we were just talking about

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:45.900
all of the bachelor fantasies right now

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:47.317
and I'm sending her videos going,

00:03:47.317 --> 00:03:48.567
"Wendy, you're not gonna believe

00:03:48.567 --> 00:03:49.837
"what's happening right now."

00:03:49.837 --> 00:03:52.420
(upbeat music)

